<http://data.silknow.org/object/87c55dfa-8cc7-3fb4-a831-51bc9aa48677/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This veil formed a boxlike cover for the chalice during portions of the liturgy. Its central image shows the young Christ blessing from within a chalice, flanked by Arabic script labeling him Jesus, the Messiah. The Greek inscription surrounding the medallion speaks of Christ’s sacrifice, while the Georgian inscriptions at the ends of the cross-arms plead for the donor, the nobleman Solomon Shavrashidze."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/87c55dfa-8cc7-3fb4-a831-51bc9aa48677> .

